{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Regal",
  "theme": "regal",
  "_about": "After a 1987 Buick Regal's dash (generated by tools/gen_regal.py, edit that): chrome-framed side pods, the left a 12 V voltmeter (8..16 V) and the right oil temperature (50 / 110 / 150 C), each needle pivoting from the pod's inner edge, with the BRAKE lamp and CRUISE under them; the centre panel holds a swinging speed needle over a straight row of mph numbers, 5 to 85 spread evenly with 55 amber right of the middle (as the Turbo 3.8's), the speed big in the VFD orange over the middle, a rolling odometer under it (the needle, a layer of its own, sweeps over it), the range with P R N D and the gear number under it in the left pod and the clock in the right, where the turn signals were, the fuel needle centred between a yellow LED boost bar (0..1.5 bar) and the LED rev bar (0..7000 rpm in 28 segments, green with each 1000's orange, a red mark above the labels from the Redline setting to the end; the fuel gauge's marks split at one horizontal line that E, the pump and F stand on, UNLEADED FUEL ONLY over it and PREMIUM FUEL under it, as the Turbo Regal's); no map window. Shader rdash plus text sheets.",
